cent you may have forgotten this gem  of a role in this is the end  the apocalyptic comedy from the minds of  seth rogen and evan goldberg  emma played a character so unexpected  you wouldn't believe it  herself in this hilarious end of the  world comedy  fictionalized versions of the cast must  reckon with the end of the world  emma played an exaggerated version of  herself trying to survive the end times  while she doesn't have too much screen  time she absolutely steals the show when  a misunderstanding leads her to turn on  her friends  to go fend for herself who knew emma had  such a knack for comedic timing  maybe it's just the incongruity of  seeing the put together actress in  survival mode  but she absolutely nails the funny in  this role i mean no  but i would say it's completely obvious  what's  one of emma watson's more overlooked  roles is nicki moore  in the bling ring directed by sophia  coppola the satirical movie based on  real events got pretty mixed reviews but  it's one of emma's most  interesting roles because it's so  different from anything else she's done  here we see emma transformed into a  vapid image obsessed valley girl who  spends her days robbing the homes of  celebrities like paris hilton and  lindsay lohan  in an interview with gq watson said that  nikki is  everything i felt strongly against she's  superficial materialistic vain and  immoral  that's why it was such a great role for  her because it showed the world what she  could really do as an actress  this has been a very difficult time for  myself  next up darren aronofsky's noah based on  the tale of noah and the ark this  biblical epic saw emma playing noah's  adopted daughter-in-law  isla she was also reunited with perk's  co-star logan lerman  although this time she plays a love  interest to douglas booth's  shem the movie had an all-star cast in  russell crowe  jennifer connolly anthony hopkins and  ray windstone  emma gives a heart-wrenching performance  in what ends up being a complicated tale  about morality  and mercy he chose you for a reason noah  moving away from the ancient epic of  noah we come full circle to  the circle a techno thriller that  focuses on a google-like tech company  with mysterious and potentially  dangerous plans  this high-profile critical flop came out  in 2017  and was based on a novel of the same  name by dave eggers  starring next to tom hanks emma played  the role of may holland  an employee of the circle who gets  involved in a mysterious one-of-a-kind  experiment that changes her life  and the lives of those around her while  the movie was a flop emma keeps  surprising with interesting film choices  what i am proposing is radical openness  and unbroken connection like this next  one  in 2015 emma starred in colonia also  known as the colony in the uk  colonia is a historical thriller that's  inspired by true events  set during the 1973 military coup in  chile the movie focuses on emma watson's  lena  a young woman who gets caught up in an  eerie and dangerous cult called the  colonia dignidad  in order to save her boyfriend daniel we  love seeing emma play the unlikely hero  swept up in events beyond her control  i've been searching for god but i  haven't found him yet  emma played angela gray in the twisty  psychological thriller  regression starring ethan hawk and harry  potter's david thwellis  who you may know better as remus lupin  said in 1990  the movie is a dark examination of abuse  the panic surrounding demonic cults  and repressed memory emma plays the teen  daughter of the main suspect at the  center of the case but spoiler alert  her character isn't quite who she seems  at first and it makes for an interesting  and unexpected performance from emma  watson  you walk around as if  everything was normal emma's voice has  become super recognizable so it makes  sense she do voice work at some point or  another  but thus far she's only dipped her toes  into voice acting  once in her career did you know that  emma starred in the animated movie the  tale of despereaux  in 2007 in between harry potter films  emma took the time to voice princess pea  in this animated adaptation of kate  dicamillo's children's book the tale of  despereaux  in the movie emma plays the young  princess who befriends despereaux a  brave mouse who embraces adventure  instead of running from it is that you  my little mouse while her big name and  star power has meant that emma is often  playing the lead  she has also done some understated work  in supporting roles like this one  emma played a small supporting role as  lucy in my week with marilyn which stars  michelle williams as the iconic marilyn  monroe  the movie follows an aspiring filmmaker  who bonds with marilyn while she spends  a week shooting a film in london  while emma only spent a few days  shooting her scenes she got to share  screen time with eddie redmayne  years before he would join the wizarding  world as newt scamander  and now it's time to search the sites a  little higher  and speaking of harry potter connections  way back in 2007  emma starred in ballet shoes a  television movie based on the 1936 novel  of the same name  she plays pauline fossil one of three  orphans adopted by an eccentric explorer  played by richard griffiths  who struggled to pursue their ambitious  dreams you may recognize griffiths as  uncle dursley himself this one is  especially notable because it was emma  watson's very first role  outside of playing hermione anyone who  goes off any audition anywhere has to  sing dance from  sight who knew that on top of being a  wonderful actress  model activist we could go on that emma  watson could also  sing she makes the perfect bell in  disney's live action version  of beauty and the beast her most  commercially successful  film since harry potter beauty and the  beast showed us yet another side of emma  watson  and yes that's actually her singing  while she said the experience of singing  was 